      "writtenOn": "2022-04-19T17:59:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What is the significance of cache line size here? Note that 16 bytes is the architectural minimum, but in practice, cache lines are at least 64 bytes.\n\nDo you have any plans to use the timer interrupt or doing any kind of exception handling when things are working as expected? Are you actually planning to use both SP_EL0 and SP_ELx at EL1? If not, you could probably simplify this code quite a bit.",
      "revId": "bfb6bc5e11bdf6e8a36dcfac490f305a0315b1f3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "610d36a8_6f157149",
        "filename": "pvmfw/exceptions.S",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 83,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-20T10:59:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As noted above, the cache line optimisation is mostly just inherited from Hafnium. It might not actually matter.\n\nI don\u0027t expect to use the timer interrupt in the pVM firmware, but I do expect David\u0027s unikernel to use it, and I was hoping to make this exception vector common shared code that can be used by any bare-metal Rust binary targeting a VM.",
      "parentUuid": "3a4b0c46_3374322a",
      "revId": "bfb6bc5e11bdf6e8a36dcfac490f305a0315b1f3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "324773bb_f9a9d117",
