    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9d9ff9b1_94b05bcf",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/exceptions.rs",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 24,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-20T10:59:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the stack pointer or memory map is messed up, that may result in another exception immediately. `emergency_write_str` seems to be more reliable as it doesn\u0027t write to memory.\n\nI ran into this quite a bit while debugging page table and other initialisation issues, where something would be wrong, an exception would happen, and `emergency_write_str` would work but `eprintln` wouldn\u0027t, and it was useful to at least know that an exception had happened even if I didn\u0027t get the ESR value.",
      "parentUuid": "a094c6fb_e24f4129",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 24,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 24,
        "endChar": 23
      },
